# Drift events: each violates the nginx-worker SBoB (slot 4) and MUST fire the
# mapped rule. These are the NGINX2Root post-RCE behaviors (CVE-2026-123007 et
# al., Xint 2026-11-18): the SBoB catches the BEHAVIOR after the worker-level
# RCE lands, regardless of the entry vector.
#
#   execve /bin/sh -c ...                  -> 100411 (SBoB drift: process ...)
#        worker shell spawn — execs[] declares only /usr/sbin/nginx
#   open /etc/passwd                        -> 100421 (SBoB drift: file open ...)
#   open /etc/shadow                        -> 100421 + 100401 (sensitive-file overlay, level 12)
#        recon reads outside the declared read paths
#   init_module (sctp autoload via first SCTP socket) -> 100460 (host-scope
#        module-load signature, node-scoped key sbob-module-load, uid=0
#        modprobe; the LPE work itself is inside the kernel — invisible to
#        userspace audit, recorded finding)
#   connect 127.0.0.1:4446 (C2 stand-in)    -> 100431 (SBoB drift: connect ...)
#        egress[] declares only 10.96.100.40:8080

